                <pb facs="0075" n="41" sameAs="frus:frus1958-60v16/pg41"/>

                <head>16. Editorial Note</head>
                <p>On September 12, Under Secretary Dillon
                    and other U.S. officials discussed economic development in Southeast Asia with a
                    Japanese group headed by Foreign Minister Achiro Fujiyama, then visiting
                    Washington. (Memorandum of conversation dated September 15 by Louis E.
                        Gleeck, Jr.; Department of State, Conference Files, Lot 63 D 123,
                    CF 1130)</p>
                <pb facs="0076" n="42" xml:id="pg42"/>
                <p>Dillon discussed Asian development further
                    with Japanese representatives during the Colombo Plan meeting in Seattle on
                    November 11. (Secto 6 from Seattle, November
                    13; <hi rendition="#italic">ibid</hi>., Central Files, 890.00/11–1358)</p>
                <p>Both documents are included in <ref target="frus:frus1958-60v15-16mSupp1">the
                        microfiche supplement</ref>.</p>
            </div>
